    "text": "{\n  \"anomaly_detected\": true,\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"anomalies\": [\n    {\n      \"category\": \"short_to_ground\",\n      \"components\": [\"U10\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U10.13\", \"U10.14\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"GND\", \"LAN_PORT3_TX+\", \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The SKW92A pins U10.13 (LAN_PORT3_TX+) and U10.14 (LAN_PORT3_TX-) are members of the GND net (net code 2), alongside the real ground pins U10.17, U10.20, U10.27 and U10.30. The LAN port 3 transmit differential pair is therefore hard-shorted to ground. Each LAN_PORT3_TX pin is also listed as a separate bidirectional pin on its own signal path in the SKW92A part definition.\",\n      \"expected\": \"LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- should be independent differential signal nets, carrying the port 3 PHY transmit signals. They should not be connected to GND. The SKW92A datasheet lists these as LAN port 3 TX pins, not ground pins.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"2\\\") (name \\\"GND\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U10\\\") (pin \\\"13\\\") (pinfunction \\\"LAN_PORT3_TX+\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\")) (node (ref \\\"U10\\\") (pin \\\"14\\\") (pinfunction \\\"LAN_PORT3_TX-\\\") (pintype \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(pin (num \\\"13\\\") (name \\\"LAN_PORT3_TX+\\\") (type \\\"bidirectional\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"SKW92A module ... 1 WAN + 4 LAN 10/100 ports\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The LAN3 transmit pair is shorted to ground. The Ethernet PHY for port 3 cannot drive or receive correctly, and the short may also load or damage the SKW92A's PHY driver. Ethernet port 3 would not function, and the switch could be damaged on power-up.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.85\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"C6\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C6.1\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(C6-Pad1)\", \"GND\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C6 is a 0.1 \u00b5F capacitor whose pin 1 is on a net by itself (unconnected-(C6-Pad1)). Its pin 2 is on GND. The capacitor is therefore non-functional. Its footprint is also an inductor pad, Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder, which does not match a capacitor part.\",\n      \"expected\": \"A 0.1 \u00b5F decoupling or bypass capacitor should have both terminals connected to the rail and ground it decouples. A capacitor should carry a capacitor footprint.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C6\\\") (value \\\"0.1uF\\\") (footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C6-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"C6\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\")))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C6 unconnected-_C6-Pad1_ 0 0.1u\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The bypass capacitor does nothing, so whichever rail it was meant to decouple lacks the intended high-frequency decoupling. The mismatched footprint may also cause placement or assembly problems.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.5\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the SKW92A LAN_PORT3_TX+ and LAN_PORT3_TX- pins tied directly to the GND net, which is a clear hard short of an Ethernet transmit pair to ground. A second, lower-confidence finding is the unconnected 0.1 \u00b5F capacitor C6, which has an inductor footprint.\"\n}",
